# Linear Workspace: Decision Making Tool

The Linear MCP is connected. Always use it to look up issues before working on tasks.

## Key IDs
- **Workspace:** UCSB Spatial Center
- **Team:** `UCSB Spatial Center` (key: `UCS`)
- **Project:** `Decision Making Tool` (id: `9f249268-5ae4-48e1-871d-7bca6ee1f511`)

## Labels
| Label | Branch / Meaning |
|---|---|
| `foundation` | Core scaffolding, services, layout — branch: `foundation` |
| `solution-controls` | Left sidebar, solution finder — branch: `feat/solution-controls` |
| `map-spatial` | ArcGIS map panel — branch: `feat/map-spatial` |
| `analysis-dashboards` | Right sidebar, metrics, comparison — branch: `feat/analysis-dashboards` |
| `aoi-dashboard` | Area of Interest panel (right sidebar); use with `analysis-dashboards` when scope is AOI-only |
| `verbal-review` | Flagged during live UI review; descriptions should use **Problem → Location → Fix** (see below) |
| `backend` | Server/API/data-pipeline work — **only add when work is not the default app/UI stack** |
| `CP1`–`CP4` | Checkpoint milestone (CP1=High priority, CP2–4=Medium, stretch=Low) |
| `stretch` | Nice-to-have; defer if time-constrained |

**Default stack:** Issues are assumed **client/UI (Angular + map + sidebars)** unless the `backend` label is present. Do **not** add a `frontend` label.

## Issue titles & numbering
- **Title:** Plain imperative phrase only — **no** `ANL-XX` / `SOL-XX` style prefixes. Linear already provides `UCS-###`.
- **Branch / area:** Use labels (`analysis-dashboards`, `solution-controls`, etc.), not title prefixes.

## Issue description template (especially `verbal-review`)

**Agent skill:** For step-by-step creation (when to use vs feature specs), see [create-linear-verbal-review-ticket](mdc:.cursor/skills/create-linear-verbal-review-ticket/SKILL.md).

Use this structure so tickets are scannable when context-switching:

1. **## Problem** — What is wrong or missing; why it matters (user impact).
2. **## Location** — Where in the app and/or repo (panel, file, element id).
3. **## Fix** — Intended direction; acceptance-style bullets if helpful.
4. **## Design / open questions** (optional) — When product/design sign-off or tradeoffs are needed before implementation.
5. **## Related** — `UCS-###` links only (no duplicate pseudo-IDs in titles).

## Shorthand Prompts
When the user types these, interpret them as:

| User says | What to do |
|---|---|
| `show [branch]` | `list_issues` filtered by that branch label |
| `show CP1` | `list_issues` filtered by label `CP1` |
| `show [branch] CP1` | `list_issues` filtered by both labels |
| `look up UCS-XX` | `get_issue` by that identifier |
| `done UCS-XX` | `set_task_status` → `done` |
| `new [branch] issue: [title]` | `save_issue` with correct **branch** label(s) + team + project; add `backend` only if not UI work |
| `sub UCS-XX: [title]` | `save_issue` with `parentId` of UCS-XX |
| `update UCS-XX: [note]` | `save_issue` appending note to that issue's description |
| `project update: [note]` | `save_project` updating the description's "Current Status" section |

## When Working on a Task
1. Always call `get_issue` with the UCS identifier first
2. Note the labels to understand which branch and checkpoint it belongs to
3. Check `parentId` — if set, this is a sub-task; look up the parent too
